Package: retrobox-labwc
Version: @VERSION@
Section: games
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Maintainer: Manu Romero <manu4.2012@gmail.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/RetroboxProject/retrobox-labwc
Depends: retrobox-core, @DEPENDS@
Recommends: @RECOMMENDS@
Description: Retrobox labwc gaming session on its own TTY
 Runs Retrobox inside a labwc Wayland session on a dedicated virtual
 terminal, isolated from the desktop session (its own D-Bus session):
 retrobox-enter-tty switches to it from the desktop, Win+D goes back, and
 the session closes itself when Retrobox exits. Includes display and audio
 output switching (Win+P, Win+O) and the labwc configuration it needs.
 .
 Installed under /opt/retrobox/labwc. Each user then runs
 retrobox-labwc-setup once to write their labwc configuration, the
 ~/.bashrc.d hook that starts the session and, through sudo, the rules for
 switching TTYs and logging in automatically.
